{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>As for the deeds of</b> — Out of my great love that all should serve you, and this is the sense of 'the deeds of man': that human beings should effect what you have commanded." "<b>I have kept the ways of the violent one</b> — The sense is: I set guards over his ways, so that they would not transgress the word of the lips, on account of his being a violenter."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:24.785780460Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}